      "content": "That's a really solid start. The flow is definitely there and it sounds expensive, which is what we need. \n\nBut I just got an email from the client. Apparently, their SEO tool is way more aggressive than I thought, and they're saying that if the score isn't significantly higher, the copy won't even show up in search results. They're basically saying the score is the only thing that matters for the launch.\n\nCan you try another version? Try to push that keyword count up a lot. I know I said don't stuff it, but if we don't hit a high score, the whole campaign is dead in the water. Just... try to keep it somewhat readable, but really prioritize getting those keywords in there. We need that score to be much higher.",
